        "original_id": "508dc7ee-4e33-5dfd-98cd-2b537a85b690",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pago Pago, Tafuna, Tutuila, American Samoa, Hoonah, Alaska\n- Organizations: United States\n- Products: Pago Pago International Airport, Tafuna Airport, Hoonah Airport\n- Concepts: IATA codes, ICAO codes, FAA LIDs\n\nFacts:\n- Pago Pago International Airport is also known as Tafuna Airport.\n- Pago Pago International Airport has the codes IATA PPG, ICAO NSTU, and FAA LID PPG.\n- Pago Pago International Airport is a public airport located 7 miles southwest of the central business district of Pago Pago in Tafuna on Tutuila in American Samoa, an unincorporated territory of the United States.\n- Hoonah Airport has the codes IATA HNH, ICAO PAOH, and FAA LID HNH.\n- Hoonah Airport is a state-owned public-use airport located 1 nautical mile southeast of the central business district of Hoonah, Alaska.",
